    54	## 5. Problems, ranked
    55	
    56	**1 → "Equivalent" is a margin effect, and three sources of error can change it.**
    57	Quote (abstract): "the registered procedure classifies R3 and C* as 'equivalent, direction R3 lower' within the registered margin of ±0.05".
    58	- **Margin.** It is 58 to 77 percent of R3's own gain (0.065 to 0.086). The estimated difference is a 32 percent relative increase (0.0856 / 0.0649).
    59	- **Search error.** The doubling check moves one cell by 0.054 (fresh3, C*, D2+H3; report line 225). That exceeds the margin.
    60	- **Markets.** A t-interval over the six market values gives [−0.013, 0.054] for D2+H3 (my computation, 5 degrees of freedom). It includes zero and crosses the margin. With the doubled-search values it gives [0.014, 0.045].
    61	- **Design.** The margin was set after development showed d of 0.027 and 0.038 (`predictions-v2.md`).
    62	- **Effect.** The paper's interval [0.020, 0.022] gives a false sense of precision. Neither "equivalent" nor "R3 lower" holds for the neighbourhood.
    63	- **Fix (analysis on existing records, plus text).** Report the market-level interval and the relative difference. Replace "equivalent" with "difference below the pre-set materiality margin".
